## Computing Hash Values

```xiom
pub interface Hash {
  fn hash(self: &Self, state: &mut Hasher);
}
```

### Implementing Hash

```xiom
pub type Point = { x: Int; y: Int; }

impl Hash for Point {
  fn hash(self: &Point, state: &mut Hasher) {
    self.x.hash(state);
    self.y.hash(state);
  }
}

fn main() {
  let mut map = HashMap[Point, Str]();
  map.insert(Point{ x: 1, y: 2 }, "origin");
  let value = map.get(&Point{ x: 1, y: 2 });  // Found!
}
```

### Hash Consistency Rule

If `a == b` is true, then `a.hash() == b.hash()` MUST also be true. This is the fundamental contract of hashing.

### Combining Hashes

```xiom
impl Hash for Person {
  fn hash(self: &Person, state: &mut Hasher) {
    self.name.hash(state);
    self.age.hash(state);
    // Order matters — different order = different hash
  }
}
```

### Why Hash Matters

```xiom
fn count_words(words: &Vec[Str]) -> HashMap[Str, Int] {
  let mut counts = HashMap[Str, Int]();
  for word in words {
    let entry = counts.entry(word).or_default();
    entry = entry + 1;
  }
  return counts;
}
```

